<file path="src/content/docs/guides/stdlib/reflect.md">
---
title: Reflect Module
description: Reference for the Lys reflect module.
---

Metaprogramming and introspection for Structs.

## Methods

| Member | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `has(struct, key)` | Returns `true` if the `struct` instance has a property or method named `key`. |
| `get(struct, key)` | Returns the value of the property `key` from the `struct` instance, or `null`. |
| `set(struct, key, val)` | Sets the property `key` of the `struct` instance to `val`. Requires the struct to be mutable. |
| `remove(struct, key)` | Deletes the property `key` from the `struct` instance. Returns `true` if successful. |
| `identifier(struct)` | Returns the name of the Struct definition used to create the instance. |
| `is(a, b)` | Returns `true` if `a` and `b` are the exact same object in memory (reference equality). |

### Examples

```lys
struct Point { x, y }
const p = Point { x: 1, y: 2 };

io::print(reflect::identifier(p)); // "Point"
io::print(reflect::has(p, "x"));   // true
```
</file>

